<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Polish, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    Informal "ty" and impersonal forms, as Polish Android apps use ("Zaloguj się", "Spróbuj ponownie"); no gendered
    past tense for the driver ("wybrałeś/wybrałaś" is avoided by rephrasing).
    "Vehicle" is pojazd everywhere; "route" is linia, and its line on the map is trasa, so "off route" is
    "Poza trasą"; "run" is kurs; "trip" is przejazd; "block" is brygada; "stop" is przystanek; "report" is raport;
    "dispatcher" is dyspozytor; "agency" is przewoźnik; "riders" are pasażerowie; "tap" is kliknij;
    "late" is "min opóźnienia", "early" is "min przed czasem"; "fleet number" is numer taborowy.
    Vehicle numbers, route names, headsigns and stop names arrive undeclined, so they follow a noun that takes the case:
    "pojazd %1$s", "linia %1$s", "kierunek %1$s" (as Polish destination signs write it), "Następny: %1$s".
    A run's start time follows "o": "kurs o %1$s".
-->
